# 基础词 Unit30
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit30核心词汇

{{license}}{/ˈlaɪsns/}}n. 许可证；执照；v. 批准}}{{You need a license to drive a car legally.}}
{{lie}}{/laɪ/}}v. 躺；说谎；n. 谎言}}{{Don't lie to me; I know the truth.}}
{{life}}{/laɪf/}}n. 生命；生活；一生}}{{Life is full of unexpected twists and turns.}}
{{lift}}{/lɪft/}}v. 举起；n. 电梯；搭车}}{{She lifted the heavy box onto the shelf.}}
{{light}}{/laɪt/}}n. 光；灯；adj. 轻的；明亮的}}{{The light from the candle照亮了the dark room.}}
{{like}}{/laɪk/}}v. 喜欢；prep. 像；n. 爱好}}{{I like reading books in my spare time.}}
{{likely}}{/ˈlaɪkli/}}adj. 可能的；adv. 可能}}{{It is likely to rain later this afternoon.}}
{{limit}}{/ˈlɪmɪt/}}n. 限度；v. 限制}}{{There is a speed limit of 60 km/h on this road.}}
{{line}}{/laɪn/}}n. 线；行；排；v. 排队}}{{Please stand in line and wait for your turn.}}
{{link}}{/lɪŋk/}}n. 链接；联系；v. 连接}}{{The study found a link between diet and health.}}
{{lip}}{/lɪp/}}n. 嘴唇}}{{She applied lipstick to her lips before the party.}}
{{list}}{/lɪst/}}n. 清单；v. 列出}}{{Please make a list of all the items we need.}}
{{listen}}{/ˈlɪsn/}}v. 听；倾听}}{{She listened carefully to the teacher's instructions.}}
{{literature}}{/ˈlɪtrətʃər/}}n. 文学；文献}}{{English literature has a rich and diverse history.}}
{{little}}{/ˈlɪtl/}}adj. 小的；少的；adv. 很少}}{{There is little time left before the deadline.}}
{{live}}{/lɪv/}}v. 生活；居住；adj. 现场的}}{{They live in a small house by the river.}}
{{load}}{/ləʊd/}}n. 负荷；装载量；v. 装载}}{{The truck was loaded with fresh produce.}}
{{loan}}{/ləʊn/}}n. 贷款；v. 借出}}{{She took out a loan to buy her first house.}}
{{local}}{/ˈləʊkl/}}adj. 当地的；n. 当地人}}{{The local government built a new community center.}}
{{locate}}{/ləʊˈkeɪt/}}v. 位于；找到}}{{The hotel is located in the heart of the city.}}
{{lock}}{/lɒk/}}n. 锁；v. 锁上}}{{Don't forget to lock the door when you leave.}}
{{logic}}{/ˈlɒdʒɪk/}}n. 逻辑；推理}}{{His argument was based on sound logic and evidence.}}
{{lonely}}{/ˈləʊnli/}}adj. 孤独的；寂寞的}}{{She felt lonely after her best friend moved away.}}
{{long}}{/lɒŋ/}}adj. 长的；adv. 长久地}}{{The meeting was too long and boring.}}
{{look}}{/lʊk/}}v. 看；n. 外表；看}}{{She looked out the window at the beautiful garden.}}
{{loose}}{/luːs/}}adj. 松的；宽松的}}{{The screw was loose and needed to be tightened.}}
{{lord}}{/lɔːrd/}}n. 贵族；领主}}{{The lord of the manor lived in a grand castle.}}
{{lose}}{/luːz/}}v. 失去；输掉}}{{He lost his wallet on the way to work.}}
{{loss}}{/lɒs/}}n. 损失；丧失}}{{The loss of the championship was disappointing for the team.}}
{{lot}}{/lɒt/}}n. 许多；一批；命运}}{{There are a lot of books in the library.}}
{{loud}}{/laʊd/}}adj. 大声的；adv. 大声地}}{{The music was too loud; please turn it down.}}
{{love}}{/lʌv/}}n. 爱；v. 爱；喜欢}}{{Love is the most powerful force in the world.}}
{{lovely}}{/ˈlʌvli/}}adj. 可爱的；令人愉快的}}{{What a lovely day for a picnic in the park!}}
{{low}}{/ləʊ/}}adj. 低的；adv. 低地}}{{The temperature is very low in winter.}}
{{loyal}}{/ˈlɔɪəl/}}adj. 忠诚的；忠实的}}{{A loyal friend stands by you in good times and bad.}}
{{luck}}{/lʌk/}}n. 运气；幸运}}{{Good luck on your exam tomorrow!}}
{{luggage}}{/ˈlʌɡɪdʒ/}}n. 行李}}{{Please keep your luggage with you at all times.}}
{{lunch}}{/lʌntʃ/}}n. 午餐}}{{We had lunch at a restaurant near the office.}}
{{lung}}{/lʌŋ/}}n. 肺}}{{Smoking can cause serious damage to your lungs.}}
{{luxury}}{/ˈlʌkʃəri/}}n. 奢侈；adj. 奢华的}}{{The five-star hotel offers luxury accommodations.}}
{{machine}}{/məˈʃiːn/}}n. 机器；机械}}{{The new machine can produce 1,000 units per hour.}}
